<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional background</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>PPAD complexity class</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In computational complexity theory, problems are categorized into classes to formally reason about their inherent difficulty and whether they are likely to be tractable. In game theory, the NP and PPAD classes are of crucial importance, as it has been shown that computing Nash equilibria is PPAD-complete <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daskalakis et al., 2009</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2009</a>)</cite> and many decision problems around Nash equilibria are NP-hard <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Conitzer &amp; Sandholm, 2002</a>)</cite>. These key results also reinforce the arguments under which finding expert policies without demonstrations can be computationally intractable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define below the PPAD class introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Papadimitriou (1994)</a></cite> and related to some of our negative results.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 9</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(PPAD class)<span id="Thmdefinition9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A search problem <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the complexity class PPAD (Polynomial Parity Arguments on Directed graphs) if and only if it is polynomial-time reducible to the End-of-the-Line problem defined as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">End-of-the-Line Problem</span></p>
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Input:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A directed graph </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> implicitly represented by two polynomial-time computation mutually inverse functions </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:V\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:V\to V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> maps every vertex </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to its unique predecessor, or itself.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:V\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:V\to V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> maps every vertex </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to its unique successor, or itself.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A source vertex </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(s)=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s)=s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(s)\neq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(s)\neq s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Output:</span><span id="Thmdefinition9.p2.1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Either a sink vertex or another source vertex.</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">PPAD problems belong to the larger TFNP class (Total Function NP), containing search problems for which a solution is guaranteed to exist (the problems are said to be total). The fundamental property that makes PPAD problems total (guaranteed to have a solution) is based on the parity argument: in any directed graph where each vertex has at most one incoming and one outgoing edge, if there exists a source, there must exist either another source or a sink. Therefore, the End-of-the-Line problem always has a solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It is believed that PPAD is not part of P, and hence PPAD-hard problems are believed intractable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>GAIL and occupancy-measure matching</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Generative Adversarial Imitation Learning introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho &amp; Ermon (2016)</a></cite> equivalently solves the following Inverse Reinforcement Learning (IRL) problem</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{IRL}_{\psi}(\pi^{E})=\arg\max_{c\in\mathcal{C}}-\psi(c)+\left(\min_{\pi\in\Pi}-H(\pi)+\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[c(s,a)]\right)-\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{E}}[c(s,a)]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>IRL</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{IRL}_{\psi}(\pi^{E})=\arg\max_{c\in\mathcal{C}}-\psi(c)+\left(\min_{\pi\in\Pi}-H(\pi)+\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[c(s,a)]\right)-\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{E}}[c(s,a)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for a cost <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> followed by standard Reinforcement Learning (RL) for policy extraction</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{RL}(c)=\arg\min_{\pi\in\Pi}-H(\pi)+\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[c(s,a)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>RL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{RL}(c)=\arg\min_{\pi\in\Pi}-H(\pi)+\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[c(s,a)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with sets <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C},\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C},\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> constrained by modelization expressivity, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}}\to\mathbb{R}\cup\{\infty\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}}\to\mathbb{R}\cup\{\infty\}</annotation></semantics></math> a convex cost function regularizer, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[-\log\pi(a|s)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[-\log\pi(a|s)]</annotation></semantics></math> the causal entropy of policy <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Their key innovation is to show that for a particular instance of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, both problems can be solved simultaneously by training a discriminative classifier <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and a generator policy <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> in a GAN-like <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goodfellow et al., 2020</a>)</cite> manner. For a non-restricted <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\mathbb{R}^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can exchange the max-min for a min-max <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho &amp; Ermon, 2016</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Garg et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and end up with the following practical optimization formulation:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\pi\in\Pi}\max_{D\in(0,1)^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[\log(D(s,a))]+\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{E}}[\log(1-D(s,a))]-\lambda H(\pi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\pi\in\Pi}\max_{D\in(0,1)^{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[\log(D(s,a))]+\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{E}}[\log(1-D(s,a))]-\lambda H(\pi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularization factor.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This problem in particular is shown to be equivalent to the following regularized state-action occupancy matching objective: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\pi}\operatorname{D_{JS}}(\rho_{\pi},\rho_{\pi^{E}})-\lambda H(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\pi}\operatorname{D_{JS}}(\rho_{\pi},\rho_{\pi^{E}})-\lambda H(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{D_{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{D_{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the Jensen-Shannon divergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the more general case, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho &amp; Ermon (2016)</a></cite> propose that imitation learning can be done by state-action occupancy measure matching problems of the form:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\pi}\psi^{*}(\rho_{\pi}-\rho_{\pi^{E}})-H(\pi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\pi}\psi^{*}(\rho_{\pi}-\rho_{\pi^{E}})-H(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the entropy regularization makes the optimal BC policy unique and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the convex conjugate of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs of hardness results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Sufficiency of state-action matching under full-state support ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Sufficiency of state-action matching under full-state support ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be two policies such that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\pi}=\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\pi}=\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will first prove that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}=\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}=\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> then prove that the policies are equal on the visited region <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">1) The policies <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> visit the same region of the space state.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose towards contradiction that there exists some <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\notin\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\notin\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability distribution, there must be an action <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\pi}(a,s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\pi}(a,s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}(a,s)=\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)\pi^{\prime}(a|s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}(a,s)=\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)\pi^{\prime}(a|s)=0</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is a contraction since <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\pi}=\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\pi}=\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}=\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}=\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">2) The policies <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are equal on their shared visited region.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We again proceed with a proof by contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose there exists <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)\neq\pi^{\prime}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)\neq\pi^{\prime}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\pi}(a,s)=\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}(a,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\pi}(a,s)=\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}(a,s)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\pi}(s)&gt;0,\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\pi}(s)&gt;0,\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)\neq\pi^{\prime}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)\neq\pi^{\prime}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, we must therefore have <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\pi}(s)\neq\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\pi}(s)\neq\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, assume <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\pi}(s)&gt;\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\pi}(s)&gt;\mu_{\pi^{\prime}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>; thus, for all <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a^{\prime}|s)&lt;\pi^{\prime}(a^{\prime}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a^{\prime}|s)&lt;\pi^{\prime}(a^{\prime}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> by the equality of the state-action occupancy measures.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is a contradiction since that would mean</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(a^{\prime}|s)&lt;\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi^{\prime}(a^{\prime}|s)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(a^{\prime}|s)&lt;\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi^{\prime}(a^{\prime}|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">but <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability distribution.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Nash equilibria for the game in Figure <a href="#S4.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Insufficiency of state-only matching with full-state support ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We want to show that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}((a_{1},a_{1})|s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}((a_{1},a_{1})|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed a Nash equilibrium of the two-player game described in figure Figure <a href="#S4.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Insufficiency of state-only matching with full-state support ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose towards contradiction that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a Nash equilibrium, as some player <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> is better off from unilaterally deviating. By the performance difference lemma (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1a" title="Lemma D.1 (Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in ( ) ). ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>), there must exists a state <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> with positive advantage</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)=Q^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})-V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s),\quad\text{with }a^{-i}=a_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)=Q^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})-V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s),\quad\text{with }a^{-i}=a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">when the player <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> chooses <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{i}=a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}=a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})\coloneqq r_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})+\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}P(s^{\prime}|s,a)V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})\coloneqq r_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})+\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}P(s^{\prime}|s,a)V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This is a contradiction since, when fixing <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{i}=a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}=a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r_{i}(a^{i}\neq a^{-i},s)-V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s)+\gamma Q^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r_{i}(a^{i}\neq a^{-i},s)-V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s)+\gamma Q^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s,a^{i},a^{-i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-1-(1-\gamma)V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s)+\gamma A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-1-(1-\gamma)V^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(s)+\gamma A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\gamma A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\gamma A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Which is a contradiction as we assumed <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\pi^{E}}_{i}(a^{i},s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Nash equilibrium.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.3 Insufficiency of state-action measure matching with unvisited states ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.3 Insufficiency of state-action measure matching with unvisited states ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof below has been extracted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al. (2024)</a></cite> and only slightly adapted for infinite horizon games.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We explicitly construct a two-player common payoff Markov Game with infinite horizon and a common action space <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}=\{a_{1},a_{2},a_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}=\{a_{1},a_{2},a_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for each agent <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>. The state space <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is countably infinite and ordered.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The action-independent (shared) reward function is defined as <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{i})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{i})=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, and <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is even. The transition dynamics are described in Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of hardness results ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="139.8" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 445.55 139.8" width="445.55"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.6pt" transform="translate(0,139.8) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(20.1,0) translate(0,68.21)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 19.69 0 C 19.69 10.87 10.87 19.69 0 19.69 C -10.87 19.69 -19.69 10.87 -19.69 0 C -19.69 -10.87 -10.87 -19.69 0 -19.69 C 10.87 -19.69 19.69 -10.87 19.69 0 Z M 0 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -6.35 -1.94)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="12.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 95.36 48.11 C 95.36 58.98 86.54 67.8 75.67 67.8 C 64.8 67.8 55.98 58.98 55.98 48.11 C 55.98 37.24 64.8 28.43 75.67 28.43 C 86.54 28.43 95.36 37.24 95.36 48.11 Z M 75.67 48.11"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 69.32 46.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="12.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 95.36 -48.11 C 95.36 -37.24 86.54 -28.43 75.67 -28.43 C 64.8 -28.43 55.98 -37.24 55.98 -48.11 C 55.98 -58.98 64.8 -67.8 75.67 -67.8 C 86.54 -67.8 95.36 -58.98 95.36 -48.11 Z M 75.67 -48.11"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 69.32 -50.05)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="12.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 182.8 48.11 C 182.8 58.98 173.99 67.8 163.11 67.8 C 152.24 67.8 143.43 58.98 143.43 48.11 C 143.43 37.24 152.24 28.43 163.11 28.43 C 173.99 28.43 182.8 37.24 182.8 48.11 Z M 163.11 48.11"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 156.77 46.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="12.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.F4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 182.8 -48.11 C 182.8 -37.24 173.