<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">This allows finding an <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Nash equilibrium which is also known to be PPAD-complete <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2009</a>)</cite>. The other direction is trivial.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.4.2 </span>Reduction for the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 5 On the Infeasibility of Tractable Lower Bounds for Exploitability ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the statement to prove
See <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 5 On the Infeasibility of Tractable Lower Bounds for Exploitability ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the result by a polynomial reduction from the problem of finding the support of an <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Nash equilibrium in a general bimatrix game to the problem of computing <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\rho}(G_{\text{bi}},\epsilon_{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\rho}(G_{\text{bi}},\epsilon_{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{bi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{bi}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that in this one-state game, the state-action occupancy measure is equal to the policy distribution. We assume <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i,j}\max\{|{A_{1}}_{i,j}|,|{A_{2}}_{i,j}|\}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i,j}\max\{|{A_{1}}_{i,j}|,|{A_{2}}_{i,j}|\}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. If it’s not the case, it suffices to divide the payoff matrices by <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the same argument for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume access to an oracle <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(G_{\text{bi}},\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(G_{\text{bi}},\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{bi}}=(A_{1},A_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{bi}}=(A_{1},A_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}\in\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}\in\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show that polynomially many calls to this oracle are sufficient to find the support of any <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Nash equilibrium of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\text{bi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\text{bi}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.4.2 Reduction for the proof of Theorem ‣ B.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of hardness results ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> described below is sufficient for this task.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Lower bound reduction</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom">Given a game <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and a target Nash precision <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Define <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{\nu}=A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{\nu}=A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}^{\nu}=A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}^{\nu}=A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Define <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1&lt;K&lt;-\max_{i,j}\max\{|{A_{1}}_{i,j}|,|{A_{2}}_{i,j}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1&lt;K&lt;-\max_{i,j}\max\{|{A_{1}}_{i,j}|,|{A_{2}}_{i,j}|\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Define <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}=\nu_{2}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}=\nu_{2}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Define <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\lVert\epsilon/K\cdot e_{1}\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\lVert\epsilon/K\cdot e_{1}\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=L((A_{1},A_{2}),\delta)\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=L((A_{1},A_{2}),\delta)\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, for a canonical vector <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div>
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Define <math id="alg1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that

<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1}^{i}\}_{a,b}=\{A_{1}^{\nu}\}_{a,b}\ \forall a,b\in[n]\setminus\{i\}\times[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1}^{i}\}_{a,b}=\{A_{1}^{\nu}\}_{a,b}\ \forall a,b\in[n]\setminus\{i\}\times[n]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1}^{i}\}_{i}=K\cdot 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1}^{i}\}_{i}=K\cdot 1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>Use the oracle to compute <math id="alg1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}^{i}=L((A_{1}^{i},A_{2}),\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}^{i}=L((A_{1}^{i},A_{2}),\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="alg1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="alg1.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}^{i}&gt;s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}^{i}&gt;s</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}\leftarrow\nu_{1}\cup\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}\leftarrow\nu_{1}\cup\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.7" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.8" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{\nu}\leftarrow A_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{\nu}\leftarrow A_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.9" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"><span id="alg1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.10" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Define <math id="alg1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that

<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{2}^{i}\}_{a,b}=\{A_{2}^{\nu}\}_{a,b}\ \forall a,b\in[n]\setminus\{i\}\times[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{2}^{i}\}_{a,b}=\{A_{2}^{\nu}\}_{a,b}\ \forall a,b\in[n]\setminus\{i\}\times[n]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{2}^{i}\}_{i}=K\cdot 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{2}^{i}\}_{i}=K\cdot 1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>Use the oracle to compute <math id="alg1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{2}^{i}=L((A_{1},A_{2}^{i}),\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{2}^{i}=L((A_{1},A_{2}^{i}),\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="alg1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="alg1.10.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{2}^{i}&gt;s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{2}^{i}&gt;s</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.11" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}\leftarrow\nu_{2}\cup\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}\leftarrow\nu_{2}\cup\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.12" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.13" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}^{\nu}\leftarrow A_{2}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}^{\nu}\leftarrow A_{2}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_many">
<div id="alg1.14" class="ltx_listingline ltx_figure_panel">Return <math id="alg1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1},\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1},\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove this fact, it suffices to note that replacing <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}^{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>ν</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}^{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,2\},i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,2\},i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> changes the value of the lower bound only if <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k,i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k,i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-Nash equilibrium <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with supports supersets of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1},\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1},\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Formally, let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{s}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{s}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of policies minimizing the Nash gap with the imitation error <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi^{s}_{\min}\coloneqq{\arg\min}_{\pi_{1},\pi_{2}:\lVert\pi_{1}\pi_{2}^{\top}-\pi^{E}_{1}{\pi^{E}_{2}}^{\top}\rVert_{1}=s}\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi_{1},\pi_{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.111em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>E</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>NashGap</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{s}_{\min}\coloneqq{\arg\min}_{\pi_{1},\pi_{2}:\lVert\pi_{1}\pi_{2}^{\top}-\pi^{E}_{1}{\pi^{E}_{2}}^{\top}\rVert_{1}=s}\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi_{1},\pi_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and arrange the set in lexicographic order of the concatenated indicator vector encodings of the supports of the two players. We show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu_{1},\nu_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu_{1},\nu_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the first element of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{s}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{s}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> which we denote <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu^{0}_{1},\nu^{0}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu^{0}_{1},\nu^{0}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a fixed player, then for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\nu_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\nu_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>: then there doesn’t exist any element with a smaller lexicographic index in <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi^{s}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>min</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi^{s}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{j}\subseteq\nu^{0}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{j}\subseteq\nu^{0}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin\nu_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin\nu_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>: then there must be an equilibrium such that player <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> takes action <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with null probability. Hence, <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu^{0}_{j}\subseteq\nu_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu^{0}_{j}\subseteq\nu_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{j}=\nu^{0}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{j}=\nu^{0}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu_{1},\nu_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu_{1},\nu_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> are valid supports for an <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Nash equilibrium.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ B.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of hardness results ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> allows us to conclude that finding <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is a PPAD-hard problem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs of upper bounds</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 6.2 Provable convergence under strategic dominance ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 6.2 Provable convergence under strategic dominance ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following the proof outline from the main text, we use the Dominant Strategy Equilibrium assumption to simplify the Nash gap as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)=\max_{i,\pi^{*}_{i}}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{*}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)=\max_{i,\pi^{*}_{i}}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{*}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can then add and subtract the expert value for every player, and apply the performance difference lemma (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1a" title="Lemma D.1 (Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in ( ) ). ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) twice:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})+V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})+V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi}(s,a)\left(\pi^{E}(a|s)-\pi(a|s)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi}(s,a)\left(\pi^{E}(a|s)-\pi(a|s)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(s,a)\left(\pi^{E}_{-i}(a_{-i}|s)-\pi_{-i}(a_{-i}|s)\right)\pi^{E}_{i}(a_{i}|s)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(s,a)\left(\pi^{E}_{-i}(a_{-i}|s)-\pi_{-i}(a_{-i}|s)\right)\pi^{E}_{i}(a_{i}|s)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the Q-functions are defined as in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1a" title="Lemma D.1 (Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in ( ) ). ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now upper bounding the Q-functions using <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert Q^{\pi^{\prime}}\rVert_{\infty}\leq 1/(1-\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Q^{\pi^{\prime}}\rVert_{\infty}\leq 1/(1-\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> for any policy <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}+\left\lVert\pi_{-i}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}+\left\lVert\pi_{-i}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2a" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> we conclude,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq\frac{(2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\leq\frac{2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq\frac{(2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\leq\frac{2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 6.3 Relaxing the dominance assumption ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 6.3 Relaxing the dominance assumption ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The key is to use a very similar construction as for the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 6.2 Provable convergence under strategic dominance ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, leveraging the triangle inequality to introduce the slackness <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using similar arguments, we apply Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1a" title="Lemma D.1 (Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in ( ) ). ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and get:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}+\left\lVert(\pi^{*}_{i},\pi_{-i})(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\cdot\max_{i}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}+\left\lVert(\pi^{*}_{i},\pi_{-i})(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Them we conclude using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2a" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> and our assumption:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq\frac{(2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\leq\frac{2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq\frac{(2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}\leq\frac{2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})}{(1-\gamma)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix ltx_pruned_first">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional lemmas</h2>

<div id="Thmlemma1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alatur et al. (2024)</a></cite>)<span id="Thmlemma1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi,i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi,i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho_{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i}(s)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho_{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i}(s)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi}_{i}(s,a)\coloneqq r_{i}(s,a)+\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}P(s^{\prime}|s,a)V^{\pi}_{i}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}_{i}(s,a)\coloneqq r_{i}(s,a)+\gamma\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}P(s^{\prime}|s,a)V^{\pi}_{i}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1a.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1a.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">And more generally,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{0})=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i}(s)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{0})=\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho_{\pi^{\prime}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i}(s)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">See proof of Theorem IX.5 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alatur et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmlemma2a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i},q_{i}\in\Delta_{m_{i}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i},q_{i}\in\Delta_{m_{i}-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be probability distributions over a discrete set of size <math id="Thmlemma2a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> isomorphic to <math id="Thmlemma2a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, note <math id="Thmlemma2a.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p=\times_{i=1}^{n}p_{i},q=\times_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\times_{i=1}^{n}p_{i},q=\times_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in[m_{1}]\times\dots\times[m_{n}]}\lvert p(j)-q(j)\rvert\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\lvert p_{i}(j)-q_{i}(j)\rvert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in[m_{1}]\times\dots\times[m_{n}]}\lvert p(j)-q(j)\rvert\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\lvert p_{i}(j)-q_{i}(j)\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed with a proof by induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The statement trivially holds for <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume it holds for <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that it also holds for <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, note <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{n}=\times_{i=1}^{n}[m_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\times_{i=1}^{n}[m_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{n}=\times_{i=1}^{n}p_{i},q^{n}=\times_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{n}=\times_{i=1}^{n}p_{i},q^{n}=\times_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j\in S_{n}\times[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p(j)-q(j)\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j\in S_{n}\times[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p(j)-q(j)\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad+q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad+q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert q^{n}(j_{1})p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q^{n}(j_{1})q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})-q^{n}(j_{1})\rvert+\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j_{1}\in S_{n}}\lvert p^{n}(j_{1})-q^{n}(j_{1})\rvert+\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\lvert p_{i}(j)-q_{i}(j)\rvert+\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\lvert p_{i}(j)-q_{i}(j)\rvert+\sum_{j_{2}\in[m_{n+1}]}\lvert p_{n+1}(j_{2})-q_{n+1}(j_{2})\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\lvert p_{i}(j)-q_{i}(j)\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\lvert p_{i}(j)-q_{i}(j)\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Numerical Validation</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To better illustrate how our theoretical insights are related to practical empirical settings, in the following, we provide the example of a game in which a tight <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> function can be estimated from data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we show two main properties empirically: (1) we show that our theoretically-derived upper bound indeed holds, (2) we show the impact of entropy-regularization on the tightest delta function estimate. We would like to emphasize though that the tightness of our upper bound will ultimately depend on the precise environment and imitation setting that is considered.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For both experiments, we consider the following Tag-Game environment:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tag-Game</span>. An infinite horizon two-player zero-sum game played on a 2x3 grid. For this game, we set <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>. For each time step <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, one of the player is the tagger, whose goal is to hit/collide with the other player who is then being chased. When the collision happens, the roles are inverted. The action spaces <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{1}=\mathcal{A}_{2}=\{0,1,2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{1}=\mathcal{A}_{2}=\{0,1,2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent actions corresponding to moving one step in one of the four cardinal directions. For each of the experiment, we consider results from all the initial states where players start at different corners of the grid. However, we reduce the number of initial states to two non-symmetrical states, while all the others can be recovered by symmetry of the game. The rewards are zero-sum, penalize the tagger with a constant reward, while also penalizing players from trying to escape the grid.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In this environment, we first compute the unique regularized Nash equilibrium <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> using a Nash Value Iteration algorithm (see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Perolat et al. (2015)</a></cite>). Then, we perturb the equilibrium at every state with different noise levels to randomly generate a set of BC policies. For each imitation policy <math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> we compute its empirical behavioral cloning error <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot 10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot 10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> episodes to estimate the expert state distribution. We can then again apply value iteration in the induced MDPs to compute best-responses and estimate a tight delta function.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>On the validity of the upper bound (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 6.3 Relaxing the dominance assumption ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition6" title="Definition 6 (𝛿-continuity of the best-response correspondence). ‣ 6.1 Characterization of Markov Games via Best-Response delta-continuity ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we compute a tight <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> by taking the cumulative maximum of the expected L1 norm between the expert and the best response, maximizing over the two players. Similarly, we compute the tight Nash gap upper bound as a cumulative maximum over the empirical Nash gaps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For this experiment, we use <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> noise levels evenly sampled from <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,0.4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,0.4]</annotation></semantics></math>, and a fixed temperature of <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> for computational efficiency. In Figure <a href="#A5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ E.1 On the validity of the upper bound (Lemma ) ‣ Appendix E Numerical Validation ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> we show how in this simple setting <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> increases when <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> increases, as well as the <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>NashGap</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21020v1/nash_delta_comparison.png" id="A5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:439/264;" width="439" height="264" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Evolution of the tight Nash gap upper bound and the tight <math id="A5.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> function with the behavior cloning error. This shows how the delta function and Nash gap tend to increase together in the simple Tag-Game environment.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This plot shows that the Nash gap tends to increase together with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Our upper bound, being greater than <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\tilde{H}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\tilde{H}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}:=1/(1-\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}:=1/(1-\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> the effective horizon, is therefore valid.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Note that in an arbitrary toy environment, the bound cannot be required to be tight. This is expected behavior as the bound is uniform on the class of <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-continuous games, thus corresponding to a worst-case scenario. In particular, the <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{H}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{H}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> factor corresponds to the worst-case expected advantage of the best-response with respect to the expert in the newly induced MDP. A similar behavior will appear with concentrability-based bounds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>On the impact of entropy regularization</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now again use Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition6" title="Definition 6 (𝛿-continuity of the best-response correspondence). ‣ 6.1 Characterization of Markov Games via Best-Response delta-continuity ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> to compute a tight estimate of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})</annotation></semantics></math> for various BC errors. Related to the ideas mentioned in Section <a href="#S6.SS3" title="6.3 Relaxing the dominance assumption ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>, we vary the entropy regularization factor and show its impact on <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#A5.F6.sf1" title="In Figure 6 ‣ E.2 On the impact of entropy regularization ‣ Appendix E Numerical Validation ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6(a)</span></a> we run the experiment by generating <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="250" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>250</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">250</annotation></semantics></math> BC policies on a large range of <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math> for the noise levels. This reveals that increasing the temperature tends to lower the <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for the simple Tag-Game environment. However, we note that fixing a game <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, this does not necessarily mean that the <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>NashGap</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}</annotation></semantics></math> is reduced by increasing the temperature, since our upper bound Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 6.3 Relaxing the dominance assumption ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is not tight for <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> in general.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.21020v1/entropy_regularization_impact.png" id="A5.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/329;" width="548" height="329" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Large range of <math id="A5.F6.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.21020v1/entropy_regularization_impact_small.png" id="A5.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/329;" width="548" height="329" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><math id="A5.F6.sf2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> at scale <math id="A5.F6.sf2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Evolution of the tight <math id="A5.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for different entropy temperature parameters. This shows that a greater temperature leads to a better control on <math id="A5.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. This behavior is consistent on the full range of <math id="A5.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> values.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The appropriate <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> scale of importance ultimately depends on the application, the trajectory budget, expressiveness of the imitation model, as well as other factors. In the tabular setting, where <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}\approx 10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}\approx 10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> is achievable with tens of thousands of examples (see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Freihaut et al. (2025)</a></cite>), the behavior of regularization coefficients remains consistent, as shown in Figure <a href="#A5.F6.sf2" title="In Figure 6 ‣ E.2 On the impact of entropy regularization ‣ Appendix E Numerical Validation ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6(b)</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For practical work, this matters because when humans are used as experts, we often assume entropy regularization to model humans’ irrationality. Having a sense of how this can also help control the exploitability of the imitation policies is therefore important.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For theoretical work, this is useful as it tells us that beyond simplifying the analysis of optimal policies, entropy regularization might also lead to better guarantees on the worst-case Nash gap.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Finite horizon case</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main content of the paper focuses on the infinite horizon case for notation simplicity. We show in this section how the results also translate to the finite horizon case. The statements are usually the same, but replacing the effective horizon <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> by a finite horizon <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. We formalize this intuition below by first providing alternative definitions for the finite agent case, and then reproving our main results.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Definitions</h3>

<section id="A6.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.1.1 </span>Finite horizon Markov Games</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A finite horizon <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-player Markov Game is defined similarly to its infinite horizon equivalent with a tuple <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},P,\{r_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n},\nu_{0},H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},P,\{r_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n},\nu_{0},H)</annotation></semantics></math>. The discount factor <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> has been replaced by a finite horizon <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, rewards and policies of this game are now time-dependent: for all <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, rewards are now denoted <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{t}_{i}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{t}_{i}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and policies become non-stationary <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{t}_{i}:\mathcal{S}\to\Delta_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{t}_{i}:\mathcal{S}\to\Delta_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The transition dynamics remain Markovian and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because of introduced time dependence, occupancy measures are usually not generalized but denote the visitation frequencies at time t of a state and state-action pair, respectively.</p>
<table id="A6.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{t}_{\pi}(s)\coloneqq\mathbb{P}(s_{t}=s)\hskip 50.00008pt\rho^{t}_{\pi}(s,a)\coloneqq\mu^{t}_{\pi}(s)\pi^{t}(a|s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:5em;" width="5em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{t}_{\pi}(s)\coloneqq\mathbb{P}(s_{t}=s)\hskip 50.00008pt\rho^{t}_{\pi}(s,a)\coloneqq\mu^{t}_{\pi}(s)\pi^{t}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This allows the definition of time-dependent value functions as follows</p>
<table id="A6.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}^{\pi}(s)\coloneqq\sum_{h=t}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{(s,a)\sim\rho^{t}_{\pi}}[r^{t}_{i}(s,a)]\quad\forall i\in[n]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}^{\pi}(s)\coloneqq\sum_{h=t}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{(s,a)\sim\rho^{t}_{\pi}}[r^{t}_{i}(s,a)]\quad\forall i\in[n],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For ease of notation we define <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi}(s)=V_{i,0}^{\pi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi}(s)=V_{i,0}^{\pi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and policy <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, the definition of value functions is extended to <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}^{\pi}(\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}^{\pi}(\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> for any distribution <math id="A6.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\in\Delta_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\in\Delta_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.1.2 </span>Assumptions on matching errors</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The assumptions on errors at convergence are adapted as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BC Error:</span> Error from directly matching the empirical distribution of the independent individual players <math id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}\coloneqq\max_{i,t}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi_{i,t}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}\coloneqq\max_{i,t}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi_{i,t}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Measure Matching Error:</span> Error on matching occupancy measures.
<br class="ltx_break">- State-only occupancy measure: <math id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mu}\coloneqq\max_{t}\left\lVert\mu^{t}_{\pi}-\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mu}\coloneqq\max_{t}\left\lVert\mu^{t}_{\pi}-\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break">- State-action occupancy measure: <math id="A6.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\rho}\coloneqq\max_{t}\left\lVert\rho^{t}_{\pi}-\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}\right\rVert_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\rho}\coloneqq\max_{t}\left\lVert\rho^{t}_{\pi}-\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}\right\rVert_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Performance difference lemma for finite horizon</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we adapt the previously stated Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1a" title="Lemma D.1 (Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in ( ) ). ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> to finite horizon Markov games. This will allow us to generalize the results of the paper in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Results ‣ Appendix F Finite horizon case ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1b" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1b.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1b.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite horizon version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1a" title="Lemma D.1 (Performance Difference Lemma, see e.g. Theorem IX.5 in ( ) ). ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>)<span id="Thmlemma1b.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1b.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1b.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1b.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma1b.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi,i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi,i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{(\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i})}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{(\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i})}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1b.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1b.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma1b.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)\coloneqq r^{t}_{i}(s,a)+\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}P(s^{\prime}|s,a)V^{\pi}_{i,t+1}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)\coloneqq r^{t}_{i}(s,a)+\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}P(s^{\prime}|s,a)V^{\pi}_{i,t+1}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1b.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1b.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1b.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">And more generally,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{0})=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{(\pi^{\prime}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{0})=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{(\pi^{\prime}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We only prove the first version. The generalization can be proven by the exact same construction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To simplify, given a policy <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> we overload the notations of the Q functions as follows. For every player <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> we denote the state-actions values of <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the MDP induced by <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}_{-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}_{-i}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{\tilde{\pi}}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{a_{-i}\sim\tilde{\pi}_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[r^{t}_{i}(s,a)+\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}}\left[V_{i,t+1}^{\tilde{\pi}}(s^{\prime})\right]\right],\quad 0\leq t\leq H-1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\tilde{\pi}}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{a_{-i}\sim\tilde{\pi}_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[r^{t}_{i}(s,a)+\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}}\left[V_{i,t+1}^{\tilde{\pi}}(s^{\prime})\right]\right],\quad 0\leq t\leq H-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, let <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq H-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq H-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Developing <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,t}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,t}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for any distribution <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{t}\in\Delta_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{t}\in\Delta_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{i,t}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{i,t}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=V_{i,t}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t})-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=V_{i,t}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t})-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=V_{i,t+1}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t+1})-V_{i,t+1}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t+1})+\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=V_{i,t+1}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t+1})-V_{i,t+1}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{t+1})+\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\nu_{t},a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{t+1}\in\Delta_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{t+1}\in\Delta_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution over the next state after following policy <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> on both sides and applying the recursion we get for the initial distribution <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{0})=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]-V_{i,t}^{\pi}(s)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi}(\nu_{0})=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}}\left[\mathbb{E}_{a_{i}\sim\pi^{\prime}_{i,t}(\cdot|s)}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a_{i})\right]-V_{i,t}^{\pi}(s)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">where we recognized <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{t}\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{t}\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging the terms gives the final result</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{i}^{\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{(\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i})}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{(\pi^{\prime}_{i},\pi_{-i})}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Results</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we reprove below our results now considering finite horizon games. The counter-examples remain largely the same, as well as the proof structures.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.1 </span>Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h4>

<div id="Thmlemma2b" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2b.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2b.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 4.2 Insufficiency of state-only matching with full-state support ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="Thmlemma2b.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2b.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2b.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2b.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a game and a corresponding expert policy <math id="Thmlemma2b.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma2b.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{E}}=\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{+}_{\pi^{E}}=\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, there exists a policy <math id="Thmlemma2b.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma2b.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\pi^{E}}=\mu_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\pi^{E}}=\mu_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2b.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\geq\Omega\left(H\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\geq\Omega\left(H\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The example provided in the main text is also valid to prove this lemma, by assuming an arbitrary horizon H.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite horizon version of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.3 Insufficiency of state-action measure matching with unvisited states ‣ 4 Impossibility results for exact measure matching ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)<span id="Thmtheorem1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a Markov Game with expert policy <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and a learner policy <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> such that even if <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}=\rho^{t}_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}=\rho^{t}_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t\leq H-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t\leq H-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the Nash gap scales linearly with the horizon; i.e., <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\geq\Omega\left(H\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\geq\Omega\left(H\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is exactly the same as in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proofs of hardness results ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, except the state space which is finite (therefore still countable).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.2 </span>Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h4>

<div id="Thmlemma3a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite horizon version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 6.1 Characterization of Markov Games via Best-Response delta-continuity ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)<span id="Thmlemma3a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the class of games with consistent bounds. This class is <math id="Thmlemma3a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-continuous only for trivial <math id="Thmlemma3a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma3a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\epsilon)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\epsilon)=2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma3a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">A similar proof to the one provided in the main text is valid for the finite horizon case. It suffices to adapt the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> for the finite horizon, ensuring we keep the property <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\pi^{E}}(s_{\text{exp}})\leq\epsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\pi^{E}}(s_{\text{exp}})\leq\epsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite horizon version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 6.2 Provable convergence under strategic dominance ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)<span id="Thmlemma4a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmlemma4a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is a (weak) Dominant Strategy Equilibrium. Then, any learned policy <math id="Thmlemma4a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with BC error <math id="Thmlemma4a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmlemma4a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq 2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}H^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">BC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq 2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Dominant Strategy Equilibrium assumption gives:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{i,\pi^{*}_{i}}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{*}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{i,\pi^{*}_{i}}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{*}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})+V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{i}\left[V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})+V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fixing <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply the Performance Difference Lemma (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1b" title="Lemma F.1 (Finite horizon version of Lemma ). ‣ F.2 Performance difference lemma for finite horizon ‣ Appendix F Finite horizon case ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>) to get:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)-V^{\pi}_{i,t}(s)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)\left(\pi^{E}_{t}(a|s)-\pi_{t}(a|s)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi}_{i,t}(s,a)\left(\pi^{E}_{t}(a|s)-\pi_{t}(a|s)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq H\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq H\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq H^{2}\cdot\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq H^{2}\cdot\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the Q-functions are defined as in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1b" title="Lemma F.1 (Finite horizon version of Lemma ). ‣ F.2 Performance difference lemma for finite horizon ‣ Appendix F Finite horizon case ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, applying the PDL in the reverse order,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{i}^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}(\nu_{0})-V_{i}^{\pi^{E}}(\nu_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[V^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s)-Q^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s,a)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s,a\sim\rho^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[V^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s)-Q^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s,a)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s,a)\left(\pi_{-i,t}(a|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i,t}(a|s)\right)\pi^{E}_{i,t}(a_{i}|s)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\sum_{a}Q^{\pi^{E}_{i},\pi_{-i}}_{i,t}(s,a)\left(\pi_{-i,t}(a|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i,t}(a|s)\right)\pi^{E}_{i,t}(a_{i}|s)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq H\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq H\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq H^{2}\cdot\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq H^{2}\cdot\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)-\pi^{E}_{-i,t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We conclude using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2a" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq(2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}H^{2}\leq 2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}H^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq(2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}H^{2}\leq 2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite horizon version of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 6.3 Relaxing the dominance assumption ‣ 6 Tractable and Consistent Exploitability Upper Bounds from Best-Response Continuity ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)<span id="Thmlemma5a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> be the learned policy, and assume for all <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t\leq H-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t\leq H-1</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\lVert\pi_{i,t}^{*}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{i,t}^{E}(\cdot|s)\rVert_{1}\right]\leq\mathcal{O}(\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\lVert\pi_{i,t}^{*}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{i,t}^{E}(\cdot|s)\rVert_{1}\right]\leq\mathcal{O}(\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}}))</annotation></semantics></math> for some function <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}^{*}\in\operatorname{BR}_{i}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>BR</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}^{*}\in\operatorname{BR}_{i}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="Thmlemma5a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq\left(2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\right)H^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">BC</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)\leq\left(2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\right)H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using similar arguments, applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1b" title="Lemma F.1 (Finite horizon version of Lemma ). ‣ F.2 Performance difference lemma for finite horizon ‣ Appendix F Finite horizon case ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2a" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ Appendix D Additional lemmas ‣ Matching Multiple Experts: On the Exploitability of Multi-Agent Imitation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NashGap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{NashGap}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max_{i}\left(\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max_{i}\left(\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-\pi_{t}(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\left.+\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-(\pi^{*}_{i,t},\pi_{-i,t})(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]\right)H^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\left.+\max_{0\leq t\leq H-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mu^{t}_{\pi^{E}}}\left[\left\lVert\pi^{E}_{t}(\cdot|s)-(\pi^{*}_{i,t},\pi_{-i,t})(\cdot|s)\right\rVert_{1}\right]\right)H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left((2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\right)H^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left((2n-1)\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\right)H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\right)H^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(2n\epsilon_{\text{BC}}+\delta(\epsilon_{\text{BC}})\right)H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
